 "content": "<!-- wp:html -->\n<aside class=\"lq-brief\" aria-label=\"In brief\"><p class=\"lq-brief__label\">In brief</p><ul><li>Laylat al-Qadr, the Night of Decree, is one night in the last ten of Ramadan, which the Qurʾān calls better than a thousand months.</li><li>The Prophet ﷺ promised that whoever stands in prayer on it with faith and hope of reward is forgiven his previous sins.</li><li>Its exact date is hidden. The odd nights of the last ten carry the strongest indication.</li><li>The guide has ten short pages, read in order, and every claim is footnoted to its source.</li></ul></aside>\n<!-- /wp:html -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Start here if Laylat al-Qadr is new to you. This page explains what the night is, what each page of the guide answers, and how to prepare when time is short.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">What the night is</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Laylat al-Qadr means “the Night of Decree”, and in English it is also called the Night of Power. The word <em>qadr</em> carries the senses of decree, measure and honour. The Qurʾān gives the night a chapter of its own, Sūrat al-Qadr, the ninety-seventh chapter, which describes it in five verses:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:html -->\n<figure class=\"lq-verse\"><p class=\"lq-quran\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">إِنَّآ أَنزَلۡنَٰهُ فِي لَيۡلَةِ ٱلۡقَدۡرِ ١ وَمَآ أَدۡرَىٰكَ مَا لَيۡلَةُ ٱلۡقَدۡرِ ٢ لَيۡلَةُ ٱلۡقَدۡرِ خَيۡرٞ مِّنۡ أَلۡفِ شَهۡرٖ ٣ تَنَزَّلُ ٱلۡمَلَٰٓئِكَةُ وَٱلرُّوحُ فِيهَا بِإِذۡنِ رَبِّهِم مِّن كُلِّ أَمۡرٖ ٤ سَلَٰمٌ هِيَ حَتَّىٰ مَطۡلَعِ ٱلۡفَجۡرِ ٥</p><figcaption><span class=\"lq-verse__translation\">We sent it down on the Night of Decree. And what will make you know what the Night of Decree is? The Night of Decree is better than a thousand months. The angels and the Spirit descend in it, by the permission of their Lord, with every matter. Peace it is, until the rising of the dawn.</span> <cite>Sūrat al-Qadr 97:1–5<sup data-fn=\"7c934804-a81b-494a-8782-db926a463118\" class=\"fn\"><a href=\"#7c934804-a81b-494a-8782-db926a463118\" id=\"7c934804-a81b-494a-8782-db926a463118-link\">1</a></sup></cite></figcaption></figure>\n<!-- /wp:html -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The chapter tells the reader three things. The Qurʾān was sent down on this night. The night outweighs a thousand months, a span of a little more than eighty-three years. And the angels descend in it with the Spirit, whom the Qurʾān elsewhere names as Jibrīl (Gabriel), so that the whole night is peace until dawn. Other verses place the night in the month of Ramadan.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The Prophet ﷺ tied the night to one act above all others, standing in prayer:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:html -->\n<figure class=\"lq-hadith-card\"><p class=\"lq-hadith\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">مَنْ يَقُمْ لَيْلَةَ الْقَدْرِ إِيمَانًا وَاحْتِسَابًا غُفِرَ لَهُ مَا تَقَدَّمَ مِنْ ذَنْبِهِ</p><figcaption><span class=\"lq-verse__translation\">Whoever stands in prayer on the Night of Decree out of faith and in hope of reward is forgiven his previous sins.</span> <cite>Narrated by Abū Hurayrah<sup data-fn=\"f9de49b1-382e-45a0-b936-81b2df55b25c\" class=\"fn\"><a href=\"#f9de49b1-382e-45a0-b936-81b2df55b25c\" id=\"f9de49b1-382e-45a0-b936-81b2df55b25c-link\">2</a></sup></cite></figcaption></figure>\n<!-- /wp:html -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Two Arabic words in the hadith carry its condition. <em>Īmān</em> (faith) is belief in what Allah has promised for the night. <em>Iḥtisāb</em> (seeking reward) is doing the deed for Allah alone and looking to Him for its reward. The standing itself, <em>qiyām</em>, is voluntary prayer at night, and the page on <a href=\"{{url:worship}}\">prayer and worship</a> shows how to begin with what you can manage.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">How to read this guide</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The guide has ten pages after this one. Read in order, they move from what the night is, to when it falls, to how to spend it.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:table {\"hasFixedLayout\":false,\"className\":\"lq-table\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table lq-table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Step</th><th>Page</th><th>What it answers</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td><a href=\"{{url:what}}\">What Is Laylat al-Qadr?</a></td><td>What the night is, and why it outweighs a thousand months</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td><a href=\"{{url:surah}}\">Sūrat al-Qadr</a></td><td>The chapter in Arabic, with transliteration, translation and explanation</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td><a href=\"{{url:when}}\">When Is Laylat al-Qadr?</a></td><td>Which nights to seek it on, and the expected dates</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td><a href=\"{{url:last10}}\">The Last Ten Nights of Ramadan</a></td><td>How the Prophet ﷺ spent the last ten nights, including <em>iʿtikāf</em> (retreat in the mosque for worship)</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td><a href=\"{{url:signs}}\">Signs of Laylat al-Qadr</a></td><td>The signs reported in authentic hadith, and what they can and cannot tell you</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td><a href=\"{{url:worship}}\">Prayer and Worship</a></td><td>How to fill the night with prayer, recitation and remembrance of Allah</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td><a href=\"{{url:dua}}\">Laylat al-Qadr Duʿāʾ</a></td><td>The supplication the Prophet ﷺ taught for the night, with its meaning</td></tr><tr><td>8</td><td><a href=\"{{url:planner}}\">Night Planner</a></td><td>Sunset, the last third of the night and dawn in your city on each of the ten nights</td></tr><tr><td>9</td><td><a href=\"{{url:faq}}\">FAQ</a></td><td>Practical questions, from worship during menstruation to time zones</td></tr><tr><td>10</td><td><a href=\"{{url:sources}}\">Hadith and Sources</a></td><td>Every narration the guide relies on, with number and grading</td></tr></tbody></table><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">The reading path. Each page also stands on its own.</figcaption></figure>\n<!-- /wp:table -->\n\n<!-- wp:html -->\n<figure class=\"lq-figure\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 720 230\" role=\"img\" aria-labelledby=\"path-t\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><title id=\"path-t\">The reading path: ten guide pages in order, with the three pages for a short plan highlighted</title><g font-family=\"var(--wp--preset--font-family--garamond)\" fill=\"currentColor\"><line x1=\"89\" y1=\"60\" x2=\"631\" y2=\"60\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1\" opacity=\".3\"/><path d=\"M631 60 Q690 60 690 110 Q690 160 631 160\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1\" opacity=\".3\"/><line x1=\"89\" y1=\"160\" x2=\"631\" y2=\"160\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1\" opacity=\".3\"/><circle cx=\"72\" cy=\"60\" r=\"17\" fill=\"var(--wp--preset--color--base)\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" opacity=\".55\"/><text x=\"72\" y=\"65\" font-size=\"15\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\">1</text><text x=\"72\" y=\"100\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" opacity=\".55\">What it is</text><circle cx=\"216\" cy=\"60\" r=\"17\" fill=\"var(--wp--preset--color--base)\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" opacity=\".55\"/><text x=\"216\" y=\"65\" font-size=\"15\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\">2</text><text x=\"216\" y=\"100\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" opacity=\".55\">The surah</text><circle cx=\"360\" cy=\"60\" r=\"17\" fill=\"var(--wp--preset--color--base)\" stroke=\"var(--wp--preset--color--accent-1)\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"360\" y=\"65\" font-size=\"15\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"var(--wp--preset--color--accent-1)\">3</text><text x=\"360\" y=\"100\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"var(--wp--preset--color--accent-1)\">When</text><circle cx=\"504\" cy=\"60\" r=\"17\" fill=\"var(--wp--preset--color--base)\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" opacity=\".55\"/><text x=\"504\" y=\"65\" font-size=\"15\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\">4</text><text x=\"504\" y=\"100\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" opacity=\".55\">Last ten</text><circle cx=\"648\" cy=\"60\" r=\"17\" fill=\"var(--wp--preset--color--base)\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" opacity=\".55\"/><text x=\"648\" y=\"65\" font-size=\"15\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\">5</text><text x=\"648\" y=\"100\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" opacity=\".55\">Signs</text><circle cx=\"72\" cy=\"160\" r=\"17\" fill=\"var(--wp--preset--color--base)\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" opacity=\".55\"/><text x=\"72\" y=\"165\" font-size=\"15\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\">6</text><text x=\"72\" y=\"200\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" opacity=\".55\">Worship</text><circle cx=\"216\" cy=\"160\" r=\"17\" fill=\"var(--wp--preset--color--base)\" stroke=\"var(--wp--preset--color--accent-1)\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"216\" y=\"165\" font-size=\"15\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"var(--wp--preset--color--accent-1)\">7</text><text x=\"216\" y=\"200\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"var(--wp--preset--color--accent-1)\">Duʿāʾ</text><circle cx=\"360\" cy=\"160\" r=\"17\" fill=\"var(--wp--preset--color--base)\" stroke=\"var(--wp--preset--color--accent-1)\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"360\" y=\"165\" font-size=\"15\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"var(--wp--preset--color--accent-1)\">8</text><text x=\"360\" y=\"200\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"var(--wp--preset--color--accent-1)\">Planner</text><circle cx=\"504\" cy=\"160\" r=\"17\" fill=\"var(--wp--preset--color--base)\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" opacity=\".55\"/><text x=\"504\" y=\"165\" font-size=\"15\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\">9</text><text x=\"504\" y=\"200\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" opacity=\".55\">FAQ</text><circle cx=\"648\" cy=\"160\" r=\"17\" fill=\"var(--wp--preset--color--base)\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" opacity=\".55\"/><text x=\"648\" y=\"165\" font-size=\"15\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\">10</text><text x=\"648\" y=\"200\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" opacity=\".55\">Sources</text></g></svg><figcaption>The reading path. The three gold steps make up the short plan below.</figcaption></figure>\n<!-- /wp:html -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">If you only have a few minutes</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:list {\"ordered\":true} -->\n<ol class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Mark the odd nights.</strong> The Prophet ﷺ said: “Seek the Night of Decree in the odd nights of the last ten of Ramadan.”<sup data-fn=\"f91fc52c-f1da-4e30-95fe-bf8acc25a7d8\" class=\"fn\"><a href=\"#f91fc52c-f1da-4e30-95fe-bf8acc25a7d8\" id=\"f91fc52c-f1da-4e30-95fe-bf8acc25a7d8-link\">3</a></sup> These are the 21st, 23rd, 25th, 27th and 29th nights. Each begins at sunset on the evening before the day of the same number. <a href=\"{{url:when}}\">When Is Laylat al-Qadr?</a> gives the expected dates.</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Learn the duʿāʾ.</strong> The Prophet ﷺ taught a short <em>duʿāʾ</em> (supplication) for this night, asking Allah for His pardon. The <a href=\"{{url:dua}}\">Duʿāʾ page</a> gives it in Arabic, with transliteration and meaning.</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Plan the night.</strong> The <a href=\"{{url:planner}}\">Night Planner</a> shows when each of the ten nights begins, when its last third starts and when dawn breaks in your city. The last third is the hour the Prophet ﷺ singled out for supplication, and the planner can add it to your calendar with a reminder.</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ol>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">How this guide handles sources</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The guide’s statements rest on the Qurʾān or authentic hadith and is cited in a numbered footnote. Qurʾānic text is taken word for word from a verified digital edition of the Muṣḥaf (the written Qurʾān) and is never retyped. Each hadith is checked against its collection before it appears, with its number and grading, and a report that cannot be confirmed is left out. <a href=\"{{url:sources}}\">Hadith and Sources</a> gathers every narration in one place.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong>From the wider network.</strong> Sister sites cover related ground in depth: the <a href=\"https://compelling-evidence.com/articles/ramadan-fasting-purpose/\">purpose of fasting in Ramadan</a> and <a href=\"https://compelling-evidence.com/articles/hadith-reliability/\">how hadith are tested for reliability</a> on compelling-evidence.com, and <a href=\"https://abrahamic-religions.com/journal/hira-and-quba/\">the cave of Ḥirāʾ</a>, where the first verses came to the Prophet ﷺ, on abrahamic-religions.com.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>When you are ready, begin with <a href=\"{{url:what}}\">What Is Laylat al-Qadr?</a></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:footnotes /-->\n",
